{{/*
  interaction-mode-babysit — "Interaction Mode" block variant for prompts
  whose primary mode IS the scheduled loop (with on-demand as the
  force-triggered exception).

  The interactive branch phrases itself as "a force-triggered run or a
  non-loop conversation; the user may be present" and frames interactive
  tools as an allowed option rather than the default.

  Consumers: github/babysit-contributions.

  For prompts that add extra bullets in either branch (autonomy criteria,
  stop-iterating hooks, follow-up guidance), do NOT use this fragment —
  hand-roll the block using `_shared/silent-notify-only.tmpl` for the
  common preamble and add your own bullets around it. Examples that need
  extras: ci/fix-ci, github/address-pr-comments, github/babysit-my-prs,
  github/check-pr-comments.

  For loop drivers marked "READ THIS FIRST", use
  `_shared/interaction-mode-unattended` instead.

  Usage:

    {{ template "_shared/interaction-mode-babysit" . }}

  The fragment emits its own `## Interaction Mode` heading — do NOT add
  one at the call site.
*/}}
## Interaction Mode
{{- if and .Session.IsLoop (not .Session.IsLoopForced) }}

**Silent mode** — a scheduled loop run; the user is not watching.
{{ template "_shared/silent-notify-only" . }}
{{- else }}

**Interactive mode** — a force-triggered run or a non-loop conversation; the user may be present.
- You may freely interact with the user using `mitto_ui_options`, `mitto_ui_form`, and other interactive tools in addition to `mitto_ui_notify`.
{{- end }}
